e $(\\pm 4,16).$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-4\\le u\\le 4,\\,u^{2}\\le v\\le 16\\}.\n$$\n\n![](images/38/387e22e062c4ff7f24d26561fe369041f11f59a2b0305f8dc7b3ce49d411031a.png)\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x}&\\frac{∂u}{∂y}\\\\\\frac{∂v}{∂x}&\\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{matrix}\\right| \\\\ &=\\left|\\begin{matrix}8&-2\\\\1&1\\end{matrix}\\right| \\\\ &=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\right)}^{-1}=(10)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D dxdy &=\\iint_Δ |\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,dudv \\\\ &=\\iint_Δ |\\frac{1}{10}|\\,dudv \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{10}\\int_{-4}^{4}[\\int_{u^{2}}^{16}dv]du \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{10}\\int_{-4}^{4}[v]_{u^{2}}^{16}du \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{10}\\int_{-4}^{4}(16)-(u^{2})du \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{10}\\int_{-4}^{4}(16 - u^{2})du \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{10}[- \\frac{u^{3}}{3} + 16 u]_{-4}^{4} \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{10}(((64)+\\left(- \\frac{64}{3}\\right))-((-64)+\\left(\\frac{64}{3}\\right))) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{10}\\left(\\frac{256}{3}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{128}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558904 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c128895-028a-5333-bd5a-8ee667b07a6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558854} {:answer/id #uuid "ca8ec194-90f6-583a-9a4b-6db556579326" :a