 ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-\\left(- \\frac{23}{4}\\right))^{2}+(y-\\frac{23}{4})^{2} & =\\left(\\frac{7}{3}\\right)^{2} \\\\ (x+\\frac{23}{4})^{2}+(y-\\frac{23}{4})^{2} & =\\frac{49}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561516 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ffa8ad3-16b7-5008-8c9d-488aa121797c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-5)^{2}=\\frac{81}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561468} {:answer/id #uuid "4b812960-ff22-5b0d-bda0-c5fc0a7dcb1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-5)^{2}=\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561475} {:answer/id #uuid "7123d6b4-e157-5c75-a9d2-c01edbc338af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=\\frac{81}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561485} {:answer/id #uuid "95fb5d52-26e1-547b-ad4a-bf700723fd65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-5)^{2}=\\frac{81}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561502} {:answer/id #uuid "cda75105-984c-5302-8bdf-26bdc89b2bbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=\\frac{81}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ffa8ad3-16b7-5008-8c9d-488aa121797c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-5)^{2}=\\frac{81}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561468} :answer-field/id #uuid "9228ed8d-daa2-585e-8fa3-73f0855cc2a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d2beabf7-e8c8-507c-bb34-ceb969b62d91" :question/problem "![](images/0d/0de50141c687bd36fc592bfdaa0d755c8838da9a81c81188ebfc6b408320405b.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(1,5)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=\\frac{9}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-5)^{2} & =\\left(\\frac{9}{2}\\right)^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-5)^{2} & =\\frac{81}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562433 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e7b951f-d98e-5a68-8472-6e057c0ab5a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e7b951f-d98e-5a68-8472-6e057c0ab5a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561628} :answer-field/id #uuid "32456fdc-62d9-5dbb-a411-ba3d281fd124" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562252} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f672b119-050a-5608-9c83-4c9132443e95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f672b119-050a-5608-9c83-4c9132443e95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562194} :answer-field/id #uuid "34f645a6-64ef-5792-b6c7-1a4f744bf319" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562253} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e333e92e-a591-5e20-9ca0-01be53fe0055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e333e92e-a591-5e20-9ca0-01be53fe0055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562141} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab8fbdbc-05a9-5707-ab78-71fcfbb42736" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562332} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2725edec-e9e4-5fb5-993b-32b7e209acd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2725edec-e9e4-5fb5-993b-32b7e209acd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561687} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0bee359-1a75-5e2f-8f5b-e36a4511f781" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4de28170-b86e-539e-8022-1a0054f8d5b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-253260" :question/problem "Let ${J}_{n}(\\lambda )$ denote an $n\\times n$ Jordan block with $\\lambda $ on the main diagonal. Fill in the missing entries in the matrix below.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3{J}_{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right))=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and a Jordan block ${J}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ we have\n\n$$\nf({J}_{n}(\\lambda ))=[\\begin{aligned}f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(\\lambda )}{2!} & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-1)}(\\lambda )}{(n-1)!} \\\\ 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-2)}(\\lambda )}{(n-2)!} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x,$ $n=2,$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nSince $n=2,$ we need to compute the first $2-1=1$ derivative of $f:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)) & =[\\begin{aligned}f\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) & {f}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\ 0 & f\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562447 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7740ff6c-f994-55ad-a058-c084db22a725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7740ff6c-f994-55ad-a058-c084db22a725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561877} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec63b2c8-7a90-5b2e-aad9-f70f82165d1c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562373}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7987b888-d840-5cef-9095-39b390eecef3" :question/math-academy-id "q-300758" :question/problem "If $p(x)=-2{x}^{4}$ and $q(x)=-\\frac{8}{{x}^{6}},$ then\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{p(x)}{q(x)}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we divide the two functions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{p(x)}{q(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(-2{x}^{4})}{\\left(-\\frac{8}{{x}^{6}}\\right)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{10}}{4} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {x}^{10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{x}^{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph $y={x}^{10}$ looks similar to an upward parabola, so\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{x}^{10}=\\infty .\n$$\n\nMultiplication by the positive constant $\\frac{1}{4}$ does not affect the limit at infinity So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{x}^{10}={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }({x}^{10})=\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562462 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c44ff17-61f3-54f4-b363-ea1bd3f109e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c44ff17-61f3-54f4-b363-ea1bd3f109e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561731} :answer-field/id #uuid "35f138a0-b129-5c92-b044-9a7f9862134f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562254} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27679f0a-767b-58cd-8144-921030108067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27679f0a-767b-58cd-8144-921030108067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561688} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cb408db-786a-5b26-a5af-0f25b4b11d35" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562260} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf0f59aa-7331-50e4-b1d5-d86e0389fe30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf0f59aa-7331-50e4-b1d5-d86e0389fe30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562098} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7e6e4e4-ba72-5524-86c2-1327a0ed5696" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8f69a422-81e0-551f-abc6-71d3ea93c826" :question/math-academy-id "q-250649" :question/problem "Find the range of the function $f(x)=-4(x-1)(x-4).$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$f(x)\\le $\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in factored form,\n\n$$\ny=a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}),\n$$\n\nwith $a=-4<0.$ \n\nBecause the leading coefficient is negative, the parabola opens downward. Consequently, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nThe two roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=4,$ and we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking the average of the roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{1+4}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=\\frac{5}{2}$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4(x-1)(x-4) \\\\  & =-4(\\frac{5}{2}-1)(\\frac{5}{2}-4) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{3}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(\\frac{5}{2},9),$ and the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,9],$ i.e. $-\\infty <f(x)\\le 9.$\n\n![](images/70/70dc863f5f089c9434d783495c31b77fd7a0ac84a852d2b32222b445f463efe3.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dad645d-0415-5658-be31-35d722e7881e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561854} {:answer/id #uuid "b7802217-fcc7-5486-bbd8-0b67e0f11610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562042} {:answer/id #uuid "c86f1ffc-4ac3-5b6a-963c-de4bf912162e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562081} {:answer/id #uuid "e20fd379-fb1a-5dbe-a692-d26f272c9382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562139} {:answer/id #uuid "f0a827f2-e12d-53fa-8215-157177df99c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\sqrt{5}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c86f1ffc-4ac3-5b6a-963c-de4bf912162e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562081} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd1bfcef-f919-5cd5-b2a5-2c3687f0610d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562343}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b33de5dd-a44b-50a7-ac6a-5ef9965fa83e" :question/math-academy-id "q-65061" :question/problem "![](images/f4/f4fdf6f8d819a4ee043b1cc3b86d795e3166ebfe181e0958246dc084c2f9c6fc.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that the $y$-coordinate of the point $P$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4},$ use the Pythagorean identity to find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $" :question/worked-solution "![](images/e2/e2c83b965f7108bff3165531446cce43006a41b9742914e8fc40c50741230427.png)\n\nAny point $(x,y)$ on the unit circle is related to the central angle $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe're given that $y=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}.\n$$\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{5}{16}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{11}{16}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we select the positive answer since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ is positive in the first quadrant. So our final answer is $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{4}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562486 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41027a8b-52ba-5683-92a3-eafe05f3ae05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561741} {:answer/id #uuid "4656ae6e-ba54-58ef-9045-3c8b22ec6431" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{{s}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561759} {:answer/id #uuid "47757023-cf17-574c-a434-8c9fe4c08b36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561761} {:answer/id #uuid "98cd6248-dbbd-5c94-8f56-d826f45e58ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561960} {:answer/id #uuid "dcec978f-3c53-5fe2-812a-19053c19675f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcec978f-3c53-5fe2-812a-19053c19675f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562132} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e578f61-c9a5-57f7-9d78-ad34f5963678" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ba7dd967-8709-5d76-b1fe-877b52dd2156" :question/math-academy-id "q-33475" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{{s}^{2}}}\\,$ given that $s>0.$" :question/worked-solution "The square root of a squared quantity can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nIn our case, we can simplify the given expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{{s}^{2}}} &= \\sqrt{\\frac{7}{s}\\cdot \\frac{7}{s}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{7}{s}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\ &= |\\frac{7}{s}| \\\\ &= \\frac{|7|}{|s|} \\\\ &= \\frac{7}{|s|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are told that $s>0,$ and we know that the absolute value of any positive number is just itself, so we have $|s|=s.$ Therefore, our final answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{|s|}=\\frac{7}{s}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562514 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dfb10a9-8436-5e35-b531-240827bbf3d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561972} {:answer/id #uuid "a534e8f3-d655-5502-bc89-53c81026a425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561994} {:answer/id #uuid "bd9c2754-dc15-56f5-8e26-d514db78cd49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562067} {:answer/id #uuid "d28d263f-fd3b-5140-9893-862b22fa936d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562111} {:answer/id #uuid "eb547a3b-90e6-5909-88af-1af5468ae682" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a534e8f3-d655-5502-bc89-53c81026a425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561994} :answer-field/id #uuid "036cd528-ad80-51a8-8b57-1c098a2a1799" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f9fda870-d2c0-5b67-a720-dd733f4059b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-105163" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}5{x}_{1} \\\\ 7{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=-11\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $(-2)$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1} & =-9\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{1}=3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(3)+2{x}_{2} & =4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-\\frac{11}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{11}{2}$ into the third equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & =-11 \\\\ -(3)+3\\left(-\\frac{11}{2}\\right) & =-11 \\\\ -\\frac{33}{2} & =-8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement. \n\nSo, the system has no solution."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562819 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f5e0c12-1df1-526a-96c6-ab0dd18cf612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-2(1)^{2}(1+h))-(-2(1)^{2}(1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562817} {:answer/id #uuid "54dcebd4-5b21-52a1-abea-45e80438c3b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-2(1+h)^{2}(1))-(-2(1)^{2}(1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562828} {:answer/id #uuid "632579ce-df9a-5c03-80b6-219fd7dfc7c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-2(1)^{2}(1))-(-2(1+h)^{2}(1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562830} {:answer/id #uuid "9fcbe737-7d67-54f0-a0af-c34445d7c218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-2(1+h)^{2}(1+h))-(-2(1)^{2}(1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562837} {:answer/id #uuid "aabfb2a7-9bda-52fd-af6a-cdfe4ba02cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-2(1+h)^{2}(1))+(-2(1)^{2}(1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54dcebd4-5b21-52a1-abea-45e80438c3b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-2(1+h)^{2}(1))-(-2(1)^{2}(1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562828} :answer-field/id #uuid "68616b5a-bbb9-56c3-8c1b-bdbfac656417" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562833}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "133d6a6b-ec9d-5351-abbd-509a18e66f7b" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=-2{y}^{2}x,$ express $f_y(1,1)$ as the limit of a difference quotient." :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by the limit\n\n$$\nf_y(1,1)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(1, 1+h)-f(1,1)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x,y)=-2{y}^{2}x,$ we have that\n\n$$\nf(1, 1+h)=-2(1+h)^{2}(1),\\qquad f(1,1)=-2(1)^{2}(1).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf_y(1,1)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-2(1+h)^{2}(1))-(-2(1)^{2}(1))}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nHere $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit, and $x=1$ is held constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562824 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f6c1947-d835-5c18-a01c-a8f81e230e0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-3(-2)^{2}(-2+h))-(-3(-2)^{2}(-2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562822} {:answer/id #uuid "65c76a03-53cd-5585-99f3-7193eb83af98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-3(-2+h)^{2}(-2+h))-(-3(-2)^{2}(-2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562831} {:answer/id #uuid "6609cbc2-741d-54fb-ac98-8aebd8de56e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-3(-2+h)^{2}(-2))-(-3(-2)^{2}(-2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562832} {:answer/id #uuid "b0aae4cc-928f-57bf-8b77-9a2911c3a705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-3(-2)^{2}(-2))-(-3(-2+h)^{2}(-2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562840} {:answer/id #uuid "ed53f686-6565-5dc4-b9f1-ccc38b09f217" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-3(-2+h)^{2}(-2))+(-3(-2)^{2}(-2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6609cbc2-741d-54fb-ac98-8aebd8de56e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-3(-2+h)^{2}(-2))-(-3(-2)^{2}(-2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562832} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cae743a-d164-5395-a90d-ce6590411561" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "33532890-70b2-5090-87ea-44260978f50e" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=-3{x}^{2}y,$ express $f_x(-2,-2)$ as the limit of a difference quotient." :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit\n\n$$\nf_x(-2,-2)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(-2+h, -2)-f(-2,-2)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x,y)=-3{x}^{2}y,$ we have that\n\n$$\nf(-2+h, -2)=-3(-2+h)^{2}(-2),\\qquad f(-2,-2)=-3(-2)^{2}(-2).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf_x(-2,-2)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-3(-2+h)^{2}(-2))-(-3(-2)^{2}(-2))}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nHere $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit, and $y=-2$ is held constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562826 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10ded65f-6e9b-5abc-af2a-f6ea15ffbc0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(-1+h)^{2}(-1+h))-(1(-1)^{2}(-1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562818} {:answer/id #uuid "1c3853fb-b9f6-5eb0-8abe-3badc14e5532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(-1+h)^{2}(-1))-(1(-1)^{2}(-1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562821} {:answer/id #uuid "5c39a581-ebf6-5756-a15b-ee8d27855840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(-1)^{2}(-1))-(1(-1+h)^{2}(-1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562829} {:answer/id #uuid "d02c0bbd-88f0-558c-ace0-1036b9f87d32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(-1+h)^{2}(-1))+(1(-1)^{2}(-1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562845} {:answer/id #uuid "f47c17a0-6a4a-5ef5-bdcd-1970900507b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(-1)^{2}(-1+h))-(1(-1)^{2}(-1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c3853fb-b9f6-5eb0-8abe-3badc14e5532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(-1+h)^{2}(-1))-(1(-1)^{2}(-1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562821} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c86581d-680b-586d-acbc-3448ad4ff62a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4ab0bfc6-d8ee-5e0d-9b62-1ad460fd0c69" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=1{x}^{2}y,$ express $f_x(-1,-1)$ as the limit of a difference quotient." :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit\n\n$$\nf_x(-1,-1)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(-1+h, -1)-f(-1,-1)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x,y)=1{x}^{2}y,$ we have that\n\n$$\nf(-1+h, -1)=1(-1+h)^{2}(-1),\\qquad f(-1,-1)=1(-1)^{2}(-1).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf_x(-1,-1)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(-1+h)^{2}(-1))-(1(-1)^{2}(-1))}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nHere $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit, and $y=-1$ is held constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562835 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "142263e2-ffc1-5971-aab7-a78e8fb89d3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3)))-(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562820} {:answer/id #uuid "3882cc29-e493-5280-8251-94acc6ea11be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3+h)))-(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562825} {:answer/id #uuid "6b6269b9-5085-5358-b7f7-9136abf836c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3)))+(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562834} {:answer/id #uuid "cc0c1ad0-0809-5caa-abd0-3c394f9b2ffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3+h)))-(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562844} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d16f5b-c575-532b-8e3a-633aa682efa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))-(\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3)))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "142263e2-ffc1-5971-aab7-a78e8fb89d3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3)))-(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562820} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0a173b9-7073-5910-96e4-56dae5d5791d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "77fe6685-0db5-512c-a146-7a7385d90d5f" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}(xy),$ express $f_x(2,3)$ as the limit of a difference quotient." :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit\n\n$$\nf_x(2,3)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(2+h, 3)-f(2,3)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}(xy),$ we have that\n\n$$\nf(2+h, 3)=\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3)),\\qquad f(2,3)=\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf_x(2,3)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3)))-(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nHere $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit, and $y=3$ is held constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562843 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d025d8c-206e-577a-a3ad-a8da0363314c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(1)^{2}(2+h))-(1(1)^{2}(2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562823} {:answer/id #uuid "9416a5b0-a192-5671-a21f-bcca2b4b0fd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(1+h)^{2}(2))+(1(1)^{2}(2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562836} {:answer/id #uuid "accb26f0-00d4-5fc7-86a2-9d0fe347e524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(1+h)^{2}(2))-(1(1)^{2}(2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562839} {:answer/id #uuid "bd4d3e99-65ec-5e5e-9088-f66e5c8b3c07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(1+h)^{2}(2+h))-(1(1)^{2}(2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562841} {:answer/id #uuid "d0c9afb2-f2db-51a6-a151-fef4c0837b25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(1)^{2}(2))-(1(1+h)^{2}(2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "accb26f0-00d4-5fc7-86a2-9d0fe347e524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(1+h)^{2}(2))-(1(1)^{2}(2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562839} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc00fb68-9f58-5d35-9fbc-d613f762f54e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c62e1658-4438-5b1a-b0a2-228bb5838b57" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=1{x}^{2}y,$ express $f_x(1,2)$ as the limit of a difference quotient." :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit\n\n$$\nf_x(1,2)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(1+h, 2)-f(1,2)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x,y)=1{x}^{2}y,$ we have that\n\n$$\nf(1+h, 2)=1(1+h)^{2}(2),\\qquad f(1,2)=1(1)^{2}(2).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf_x(1,2)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(1+h)^{2}(2))-(1(1)^{2}(2))}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nHere $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit, and $y=2$ is held constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563646 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "193c9dde-df02-57fb-9a38-2e3ada1317a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563003} {:answer/id #uuid "45670d3d-36e3-540d-bd5e-bd76637818f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563100} {:answer/id #uuid "7f53d534-d2c5-55c9-bc0b-0b43335f20b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563225} {:answer/id #uuid "a475de87-e762-598f-af2f-5e440020dd19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563317} {:answer/id #uuid "ff07e237-c85a-5da5-b75b-ecc1a90cc0ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45670d3d-36e3-540d-bd5e-bd76637818f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563100} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfed377d-f55c-58f7-a40b-072a8729a585" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "04b365f6-2d57-5574-aec1-e0a7c1397133" :question/math-academy-id "q-84911" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of $y=\\frac{1}{3}(k-x)(5x+3k)$ is $x=\\frac{1}{10}.$ The value of $k=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{1}{10},$ we will set our result equal to $\\frac{1}{10}.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=\\frac{1}{3}(k-x)(5x+3k),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=k$ and ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{3k}{5}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(k-\\frac{3k}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{5k}{5}-\\frac{3k}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{2k}{5}\\right)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{1}{10}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{5} & =\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563651 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09596fbb-5f17-590f-b8c6-41aea4206883" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡\\left(\\frac{3x+2}{4}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562958} {:answer/id #uuid "85052561-0afa-5d49-a8cd-46da05f90e90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡\\left(\\frac{3x+2}{4}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563244} {:answer/id #uuid "8adcb99e-b119-5618-808f-7b0725c00dbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563254} {:answer/id #uuid "e08a4d2f-d017-5f6c-b6cc-e8a0f88c0fb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563438} {:answer/id #uuid "e861d624-48ec-543a-aaf6-deee37e2e5ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡\\left(\\frac{3x+2}{4}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85052561-0afa-5d49-a8cd-46da05f90e90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡\\left(\\frac{3x+2}{4}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563244} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fbff315-ecc9-5c1a-aaa6-d1781060ca7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563564}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1369cbfd-a46c-5064-baa1-cbe5720fb540" :question/math-academy-id "q-97910" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{16-(3x+2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{16-(3x+2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{16-16(\\frac{1}{16}(3x+2)^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{16}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{1}{4}(3x+2))}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\frac{1}{4}(3x+2).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{4}{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{16}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{1}{4}(3x+2))}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{16}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcoth}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡\\left(\\frac{3x+2}{4}\\right)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that this result is subject to the condition $|\\frac{3x+2}{4}|>1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563656 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a92a5b0-f742-5f72-9fed-2fa17746b3d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,i-2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563076} {:answer/id #uuid "e312bb41-87f9-5deb-9841-5b5f28418294" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563445} {:answer/id #uuid "e72b0968-76fc-5d45-85c7-a1f5300ad455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563457} {:answer/id #uuid "fa10a00d-f989-5e31-96e2-3b5966e8e36b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563506} {:answer/id #uuid "fc7c1f10-9c81-523f-bfa3-f0d613a444d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e312bb41-87f9-5deb-9841-5b5f28418294" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563445} :answer-field/id #uuid "3db3d25b-6794-5819-bf20-9d7f989372fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563558}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "19ce6755-ce5c-5344-86b9-dca6271615dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-132608" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=0.$ Given that the point $P(\\frac{1}{2},0,1)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=(y+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)$, which of the following gives a tangent vector to $C$ at $P?$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $y=0.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(\\frac{1}{2},0).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ at $(\\frac{1}{2},0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(\\frac{1}{2},0) & =(0+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot \\frac{1}{2})+2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 0)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) \\\\  & =0+1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(\\frac{1}{2},0) & ={f}_{x}(\\frac{1}{2},0)(x-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ z-1 & =1(x-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ z-1 & =x-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ z & =x+\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(\\frac{1}{2},0,1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=0 \\\\ z=x+\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $y=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,1,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=x+\\frac{1}{2}$ (or $x-z+\\frac{1}{2}=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,0,-1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨0,1,0⟩\\times ⟨1,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $-i-k$ is parallel to the tangent line, then $-(-i-k)=i+k$ is also parallel to it."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563658 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07fa6bb7-d0f9-5e18-9b3c-e212aeb79600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562955} {:answer/id #uuid "29f5c5e8-ff02-5056-940b-e508ad765aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,4)\\cup (4,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563040} {:answer/id #uuid "541e6159-1300-54d2-9ca7-82d337be42a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,0)\\cup (0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563135} {:answer/id #uuid "96a3c878-7b87-5ad8-a727-56d45e5d6afd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[0,4)\\cup (4,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563280} {:answer/id #uuid "f50708b8-5d3c-5122-8662-e4f8a58bf6f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29f5c5e8-ff02-5056-940b-e508ad765aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,4)\\cup (4,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563040} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f7ff639-4ca5-57e6-a7d3-21f3b2dfb18a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563540}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "22fc3cb9-9f8c-550e-b1a7-090b46545ee2" :question/math-academy-id "q-70566" :question/problem "Determine the interval on which the function $f(t)=\\sqrt{t}\\,i+\\frac{1}{t-4}\\,j-5{t}^{2}\\,k$ is differentiable." :question/worked-solution "The vector-valued function $f(t)$ is defined on the interval $[0,4)\\cup (4,\\infty ).$ Let's study the differentiability of its components on this interval one-by-one.\n\n- The derivative of  $\\sqrt{t}$ is\n\n$$\n{(\\sqrt{t})}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}.\n$$\n\n \nSince the derivative is not defined at $t=0,$ we conclude that  $\\sqrt{t}$ is not differentiable at this point.\n\n- The derivative of  $\\frac{1}{t-4}$ is\n\n$$\n{\\left(\\frac{1}{t-4}\\right)}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{(t-4)^{2}}.\n$$\n\n \nSince the derivative is defined for all the points on the interval $[0,4)\\cup (4,\\infty ),$ we conclude that  $\\frac{1}{t-4}$ is differentiable on this interval.\n\n- The derivative of  $-5{t}^{2}$ is\n\n$$\n{(-5{t}^{2})}^{′}=-10t.\n$$\n\n \nSince the derivative is defined for all the points on the interval $[0,4)\\cup (4,\\infty ),$ we conclude that  $-5{t}^{2}$ is differentiable on this interval.\n\nTaking into account that all the components of $f(t)$ are differentiable for all the points on the interval $[0,4)\\cup (4,\\infty ),$ except the point $t=0,$ we conclude that $f(t)$  is differentiable on $(0,4)\\cup (4,\\infty ).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563662 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4696a05b-aa71-5436-909d-4ad6cc69953d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563104} {:answer/id #uuid "4d2524ac-5a9e-5166-a59a-c4b1cc71b052" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{41}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563116} {:answer/id #uuid "830ff5aa-499a-5e23-8b6c-9f66271ff7d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{39}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563237} {:answer/id #uuid "d146c1fe-0d81-525c-ab3e-04de8c098617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{39}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563404} {:answer/id #uuid "e4967a7e-ba74-5964-80d2-08e8ecb2bbc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{41}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4967a7e-ba74-5964-80d2-08e8ecb2bbc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{41}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563447} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1f9bfc4-206c-5615-9e86-3cd20425df2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2cd66931-0513-5d1c-9823-4729248ee301" :question/math-academy-id "q-32979" :question/problem "Find the limit ${lim}_{t\\to 1}‖f(t)‖$, if $f(t)=\\frac{4+t}{5}\\,i+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)}{{t}^{2}-1}\\,j+\\sqrt{9t}\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t) & =({lim}_{t\\to 1}\\frac{4+t}{5})\\,i+({lim}_{t\\to 1}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)}{{t}^{2}-1})\\,j+({lim}_{t\\to 1}\\sqrt{9t})\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one-by-one.\n\n- For the first component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\frac{4+t}{5} & =\\frac{4+1}{5}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second component can be found using a special limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)}{{t}^{2}-1} & ={lim}_{t\\to 1}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)}{(t-1)(t+1)} \\\\  & =({lim}_{t\\to 1}\\frac{1}{t+1})\\cdot ({lim}_{t\\to 1}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)}{t-1}) \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{1}{1+1}\\right)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\sqrt{9t} & =\\sqrt{9(1)}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t)=i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+3\\,k.$\n\nFinally, the limit of $‖f(t)‖$ as $t$ approaches $1$ is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}‖f(t)‖ & =‖{lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+3\\,k‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4}+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{41}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{41}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563664 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e7082bf-94bc-5f95-a646-926615cd1b1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-{e}^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563123} {:answer/id #uuid "5f6847e3-eb2c-5cc6-9cd0-83733cfef02d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563164} {:answer/id #uuid "873d5f29-f5c3-5d96-8997-2e96d20efdab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563247} {:answer/id #uuid "8ccbdb14-9c0c-5f46-a3d4-ae2fd1da959c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563262} {:answer/id #uuid "920aaecc-64b5-5927-be63-43fbf263f51a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "873d5f29-f5c3-5d96-8997-2e96d20efdab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563247} :answer-field/id #uuid "b24006f7-dcb6-5a3e-962f-d3babb6d995e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "33768c70-a4a8-56c5-b929-58df88c6ba1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-78268" :question/problem "Find the limit ${lim}_{t\\to 1}[f(t)\\cdot g(t)]$ given that $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are defined as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t-1} \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t}{t} \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t}{t}\\end{aligned}],\\,g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{t}^{2}-2t+1}{t+1} \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t}{t+1} \\\\ \\frac{{e}^{t+1}}{t+1}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t-1}\\right) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,\\left(\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t}{t}\\right) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,\\left(\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t}{t}\\right)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,\\left(\\frac{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)^{′}}{(t-1)^{′}}\\right) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,\\left(\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t}{t}\\right) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,\\left(\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t}{t}\\right)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi }{1} \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi }{1}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that for the first component of ${lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t)$ we used L'Hopital's Rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}g(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}-2t+1}{t+1} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t}{t+1} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}\\,\\frac{{e}^{t+1}}{t+1}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{1}^{2}-2\\cdot 1+1}{1+1} \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+1}{1+1} \\\\ \\frac{{e}^{1+1}}{1+1}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}[f(t)\\cdot g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t)\\cdot {lim}_{t\\to 1}g(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+0\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563668 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a472c55-b621-565c-b578-f92c20cbb266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arsech}⁡\\left(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563146} {:answer/id #uuid "6b7d1c78-ae26-55ef-86e8-9c531b3f1a3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡\\left(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563193} {:answer/id #uuid "bf7b4cd4-4878-5393-9a31-5c5c09f3bcdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡\\left(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563367} {:answer/id #uuid "ddb986c7-c26a-5de1-8745-8a63847438c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡\\left(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563431} {:answer/id #uuid "fba7141a-d135-5744-8bbd-0158aa2f9308" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡\\left(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fba7141a-d135-5744-8bbd-0158aa2f9308" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡\\left(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563508} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b36eef3-f0c2-5b45-97f7-a2607c73a159" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38a6fd7f-85a4-5b9d-9914-3bd5a2ab420c" :question/math-academy-id "q-97904" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{|x-5|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-10x+27}}\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-10x+27 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5x+{5}^{2}-{5}^{2}+27 \\\\  & =(x-5)^{2}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{|x-5|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-10x+27}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{|x-5|\\sqrt{2+(x-5)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}|\\sqrt{2+2{\\left(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int \\frac{1}{|\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}|\\sqrt{1+{\\left(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int \\frac{1}{|\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}|\\sqrt{1+{\\left(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)}^{2}}}\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡\\left(\\frac{x-5}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563687 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e6dbddc-14bc-525e-8243-43d97f13d5de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563160} {:answer/id #uuid "647eb414-70e2-51df-bace-381aeabfab1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563176} {:answer/id #uuid "8af33f3e-47b0-5222-adb2-0e369970c083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563255} {:answer/id #uuid "a03c2c09-7f10-51f5-b6e9-049c1b7317c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563305} {:answer/id #uuid "c9bdd2b2-810c-5ef0-84b0-8ece0783d384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "647eb414-70e2-51df-bace-381aeabfab1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563176} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd0c0893-97b7-5c87-8979-00978834031e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4e141666-84d5-5edd-9a4e-a7cb3e788f33" :question/math-academy-id "q-132581" :question/problem "A surface $S$ is defined by $z=f(x,y).$ The curve $C$ is the intersection of $S$ with the plane $x=2.$ Given that the point $P$ with $y$-coordinate $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy-\\frac{\\pi }{3})$, find the slope of the tangent to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point where $y=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(2,\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(2,\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(2,\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563689 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "189ec891-a762-54dd-8e28-66f7d86f7621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563000} {:answer/id #uuid "a937d5cd-9309-5b00-a446-cdfd649551b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563326} {:answer/id #uuid "b2d80ddb-b0ea-50ab-81d2-6892d56e013c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563340} {:answer/id #uuid "cd1cc6cd-5009-53a5-9550-f7f07275d8a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563398} {:answer/id #uuid "e69a9ba3-ccae-56d8-8e5f-5d06921f70e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd1cc6cd-5009-53a5-9550-f7f07275d8a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563398} :answer-field/id #uuid "45ab83aa-a438-50c5-87d1-85ddbe0b15e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "56172e38-6320-5f34-8b75-aab1067f37e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-86543" :question/problem "Consider the function $g(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).$ What is the rate of change of $g(x,y)$ at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},4)$ in the direction in which the function increases most rapidly?" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $g(x,y)$ increases most rapidly in the direction of its gradient at that point.\n\nIn our case, we compute $∇g(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,g(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,\\,\\frac{2}{y}⟩ \\\\ ∇\\,g(\\frac{\\pi }{4},4) & =⟨-\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,\\frac{2}{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the rate of change of $g(x,y)$ at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},4)$ in the direction of $∇g(\\frac{\\pi }{4},4)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖∇\\,g(\\frac{\\pi }{4},4)‖ & =‖⟨-1,\\frac{1}{2}⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563701 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ebf46c9-f938-50a8-9cc1-97df4784c6aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ebf46c9-f938-50a8-9cc1-97df4784c6aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563161} :answer-field/id #uuid "79bc61fa-11bd-5db1-aa6e-3d865e60342d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6e6642fc-4b0f-571e-8c66-e87cc2512b11" :question/math-academy-id "q-220354" :question/problem "![](images/bd/bd46cb7a3139ccb19b7f65bab927ef8c56ba075520262649d6fa196cdab8cc81.png)\n\nThe graph above shows a parabola. The $x$-coordinates of $A$ and $B$ are $-\\frac{16}{5}$ and $\\frac{5}{2},$ respectively.  Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola.\n\nThe axis of symmetry is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We're given that the roots of the parabola are \n ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{16}{5}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{5}{2}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{16}{5}+\\frac{5}{2})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{32}{10}+\\frac{25}{10})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(-\\frac{7}{10}\\right)}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{7}{20}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563716 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "206b7aff-d2d1-5f6a-add6-b653f58dc164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563018} {:answer/id #uuid "60f53833-01a7-51b3-b367-c22fe50326ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563170} {:answer/id #uuid "a0d74bba-4689-5ebb-920d-944005be742c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563307} {:answer/id #uuid "c5495620-9d83-5275-9d56-bcfc0407808d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563379} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f6b4d0-5d37-52d1-8795-c9a0b9d298d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5495620-9d83-5275-9d56-bcfc0407808d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563379} :answer-field/id #uuid "a738fbe9-b746-555f-a431-6ff37c754328" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563610}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9a567a48-e070-587a-94df-8a2d7148a763" :question/math-academy-id "q-32976" :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{s\\to 0}‖f(s)‖$, if $f(s)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{s}{(s+1)^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡s}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s}{2{s}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\,.$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}f(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{s}{(s+1)^{2}} \\\\ {lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡s}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ {lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s}{2{s}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one-by-one.\n\n- For the first component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{s}{(s+1)^{2}} & =\\frac{0}{(0+1)^{2}}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second component can be found using a special limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡s}{{s}^{2}} & ={lim}_{s\\to 0}{\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡s}{s}\\right)}^{2} \\\\  & ={({lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡s}{s})}^{2} \\\\  & ={1}^{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third component can be found using L'Hopital's Rule twice:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s}{2{s}^{2}} & ={lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)}^{″}}{{(2{s}^{2})}^{″}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡s}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{s\\to 0}f(s)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1/4\\end{aligned}]\\,.$\n\nFinally, the limit of $‖f(s)‖$ as $s$ approaches $0$ is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}‖f(s)‖ & =‖{lim}_{s\\to 0}f(s)‖ \\\\  & =‖[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1/4\\end{aligned}]‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563720 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cb145f1-f9ae-5d5e-9acb-c2e8557eb522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡\\left(\\frac{x+2}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562967} {:answer/id #uuid "259a3844-82ae-5b24-a85f-f38b2f21f870" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡\\left(\\frac{x+2}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563031} {:answer/id #uuid "4e03b87e-8d9e-547f-803e-f3b920ae8222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡\\left(\\frac{x+2}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563122} {:answer/id #uuid "aa279346-be14-5108-9c91-ebb49fea3432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡\\left(\\frac{x+2}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563328} {:answer/id #uuid "bb94fb36-58d4-5f5c-9e67-67e40c60505c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{arsech}⁡\\left(\\frac{x+2}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa279346-be14-5108-9c91-ebb49fea3432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡\\left(\\frac{x+2}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563328} :answer-field/id #uuid "0526b46b-564d-561d-a9aa-fedc41539160" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563520}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a95ee677-1642-5975-8b50-8432d56de160" :question/math-academy-id "q-97770" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{(x+2)\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-4x}}\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-4x & =-({x}^{2}+4x) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =-((x+2)^{2}-4) \\\\  & =4-(x+2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{(x+2)\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-4x}}\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{(x+2)\\sqrt{4-(x+2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{2(x+2)\\sqrt{1-{\\left(\\frac{x+2}{2}\\right)}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x+2}{2}\\right)\\sqrt{1-{\\left(\\frac{x+2}{2}\\right)}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\frac{x+2}{2}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=2\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{(x+2)\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-4x}}\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x+2}{2}\\right)\\sqrt{1-{\\left(\\frac{x+2}{2}\\right)}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{u\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡\\left(\\frac{x+2}{2}\\right)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563735 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "142bb8d7-2c5b-5aff-a641-87db92de52c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562986} {:answer/id #uuid "169d9c2b-ed8e-5399-9665-91d1666641d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562994} {:answer/id #uuid "29e329a9-3422-59f4-82ad-91d038159e57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563039} {:answer/id #uuid "404a6d55-06c7-5863-9890-05c5ef448ad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563093} {:answer/id #uuid "80b7f6d3-2e98-5ccb-856a-d66a6512df21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "142bb8d7-2c5b-5aff-a641-87db92de52c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562986} :answer-field/id #uuid "329e691a-a395-50ed-b83a-cc3c4efd7434" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563549}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd5e69ab-4017-5036-a080-1d135b13f5a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-84902" :question/problem "Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(6x-1)(3x+1).$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation $y=(6x-1)(3x+1),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{6}$ and ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{3})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{2}{6})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(-\\frac{1}{6}\\right)}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{1}{12}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563741 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00433fb2-2689-50b6-b5ae-b3213b484e7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562937} {:answer/id #uuid "81f0d8bc-19f0-5e3d-ad6f-8e1c66829afd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563232} {:answer/id #uuid "bc4239ca-8453-592c-a801-dc055bf9ad37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563360} {:answer/id #uuid "c97f5424-984d-5602-8981-349f5455aec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563389} {:answer/id #uuid "da9987fb-7331-55ac-8916-60a446822552" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da9987fb-7331-55ac-8916-60a446822552" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563423} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa2be9cd-8e25-5c22-a57c-dbf36efef798" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d5075c32-f624-572f-a2d3-78616466d14e" :question/math-academy-id "q-86430" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=(2{x}^{2}-y)^{2}$ at the point $A(-1,1)$ in the direction towards the point $B(-2,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)=∇f(a,b)\\cdot u\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the direction vector and the corresponding unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨-2,2⟩-⟨-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,1⟩ \\\\ u & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}}{‖\\overset{\\to }{AB}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}}⟨-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $A(-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}-y)^{2},\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}-y)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨16{x}^{3}-8xy,\\,2y-4{x}^{2}⟩ \\\\ ∇f(-1,1) & =⟨16(-1)^{3}-8(-1)(1),\\,2(1)-4(-1)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{u}^{′}(-1,1) & =∇f(-1,1)\\cdot u \\\\  & =⟨-8,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =(-8)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)-2\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563743 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "014d7fc8-5099-5882-8aa1-ded2fbbcf5aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f(t)$ and $g(t)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562941} {:answer/id #uuid "1662f69d-0d6b-5863-8f09-5d9d05419260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All the functions are differentiable on $(\\pi ,2\\pi )$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562992} {:answer/id #uuid "5fdede5d-fa26-5289-a238-94143dcae14e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f(t)$ and $h(t)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563165} {:answer/id #uuid "9706168f-6882-59ce-be20-eefcba9f53d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$g(t)$ and $h(t)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563284} {:answer/id #uuid "dab073b4-14ff-58ad-bfaa-7282357cb131" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the functions are differentiable on $(\\pi ,2\\pi )$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1662f69d-0d6b-5863-8f09-5d9d05419260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All the functions are differentiable on $(\\pi ,2\\pi )$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562992} :answer-field/id #uuid "24c4782e-d988-5b6a-b328-68cc3dd0adb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d69b9419-ecda-5adb-b076-9a4d08de1698" :question/math-academy-id "q-32701" :question/problem "Which of the following vector-valued functions are differentiable with respect to $t$ on $t\\in (\\pi ,2\\pi )?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨{sin}^{2}⁡t,\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨t\\sqrt{t},\\,1-{t}^{2},\\,t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩ \\\\ h(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,2t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "All of these vector-valued functions are defined for all  $t\\in (\\pi ,2\\pi ).$ \n\nA function is differentiable on the interval $(\\pi ,2\\pi )$ if and only if each of its component functions is differentiable on that interval. \n\nLet's now consider the functions one-by-one.\n\n- We differentiate $f(t)$ to find ${f}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({sin}^{2}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince each component of ${f}^{′}(t)$ is defined for all  $t\\in (\\pi ,2\\pi )$, we conclude that $f(t)$ is differentiable on this interval.\n\n- Next, we differentiate $g(t)$ to find ${g}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{1/2},\\,-2t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t},\\,-2t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince each component of  ${g}^{′}(t)$ is defined for all  $t\\in (\\pi ,2\\pi )$, we have that $g(t)$ is differentiable on this interval.\n\n- Finally, we differentiate $h(t)$ to find ${h}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,2,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince each component of  ${h}^{′}(t)$ is defined for all $t\\in (\\pi ,2\\pi )$, we conclude that $h(t)$ is differentiable on this interval.\n\nTherefore, the answer is: \n\n$\\,$ All the functions are differentiable on $(\\pi ,2\\pi ).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563744 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1065a3b5-7eb0-5108-b4e2-8a64406d6063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡\\left(\\frac{x+3}{3}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562978} {:answer/id #uuid "39d34837-ebfe-5409-b1ab-da122aa01d5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡\\left(\\frac{x+3}{3}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563075} {:answer/id #uuid "4c246a52-305e-5adb-972f-c828583b7f6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡\\left(\\frac{x+3}{3}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563115} {:answer/id #uuid "7b8de859-a1f8-5dd2-834f-fa91b60b37c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{arsech}⁡\\left(\\frac{x+3}{3}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563215} {:answer/id #uuid "b61c450a-f091-5a01-bd84-81b3a853a9d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡\\left(\\frac{x+3}{3}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39d34837-ebfe-5409-b1ab-da122aa01d5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡\\left(\\frac{x+3}{3}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563075} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1d9e3fb-7750-5a4b-a417-c4a5e9cfd326" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563606}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d6b27f7b-e94e-5d63-abcb-feb8d8bed4dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-97777" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{3}{(x+3)\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-6x}}\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-6x & =-({x}^{2}+6x) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2}-{3}^{2}) \\\\  & =-((x+3)^{2}-9) \\\\  & =9-(x+3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{(x+3)\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-6x}}\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{(x+3)\\sqrt{9-{(x+3)}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x+3}{3}\\right)\\sqrt{9-9{\\left(\\frac{x+3}{3}\\right)}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x+3}{3}\\right)\\sqrt{1-{\\left(\\frac{x+3}{3}\\right)}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\frac{x+3}{3}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=3\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{(x+3)\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-6x}}\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x+3}{3}\\right)\\sqrt{1-{\\left(\\frac{x+3}{3}\\right)}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡\\left(\\frac{x+3}{3}\\right)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563746 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05ed7714-762b-563c-aa6e-395fc6bb299a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562950} {:answer/id #uuid "12226c0d-85bd-508b-82d8-13bf97d8f83b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562981} {:answer/id #uuid "3bd14c1c-2112-52ab-bcdc-5d7b174123b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563079} {:answer/id #uuid "55af48ee-55a1-5c40-847d-5742b568cea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563140} {:answer/id #uuid "f8844c5c-08d4-51a1-8c11-9ac8c49c3885" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05ed7714-762b-563c-aa6e-395fc6bb299a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562950} :answer-field/id #uuid "707a53ec-3f89-531c-a47b-914f51a9c97c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "da0e0865-56b2-565d-ac33-deaee1268cf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-84903" :question/problem "Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(7-5x)(x+1).$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation $y=(7-5x)(x+1),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=\\frac{7}{5}$ and ${x}_{2}=-1.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{7}{5}-1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{7}{5}-\\frac{5}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{1}{5}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563756 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "097ae540-a1c3-563f-958f-879f687d07c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562959} {:answer/id #uuid "27ed339f-1ba9-5371-b98d-4f3e5a4957d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563033} {:answer/id #uuid "4b16ec7e-f0ec-57c4-b0d0-1fe68110981c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563110} {:answer/id #uuid "7356e8b2-c698-5246-b83e-adcafee91941" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563201} {:answer/id #uuid "7375c3cd-5447-5289-b4b3-d26964bf0961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no real solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "097ae540-a1c3-563f-958f-879f687d07c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562959} :answer-field/id #uuid "76b0b8d7-ead0-5e0b-96f7-c011cf47b3ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ee997e26-088f-52b1-8913-d296b8992e92" :question/math-academy-id "q-91348" :question/problem "Find the real solution to the equation ${x}^{7}=-\\frac{1}{128}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this equation by taking the $7$th root of each side and solving for $x.$ Since $n=7$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{7} & =-\\frac{1}{128} \\\\ \\sqrt[7]{{x}^{7}} & =\\sqrt[7]{\\left(-\\frac{1}{128}\\right)} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt[7]{{\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{7}} \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-\\frac{1}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563763 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57ea209f-e155-526a-94ca-0d966c493e42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,i+\\frac{1}{4}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563141} {:answer/id #uuid "96c6d7cb-49e7-5e45-b566-508c8a442dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\,i-2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563281} {:answer/id #uuid "9f5e6c1e-a123-5805-9a48-ff55d4732a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\,i-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563304} {:answer/id #uuid "b3791795-25ea-52db-9a06-ea2ad48e2ced" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,i-\\frac{1}{2}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563341} {:answer/id #uuid "d18ea431-dd2b-59ac-94dc-2a47eca46a91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\,i-\\frac{1}{2}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96c6d7cb-49e7-5e45-b566-508c8a442dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\,i-2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563281} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe69802c-24d6-5c9a-b43c-e07a25e5de2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563641}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ffacb628-f280-51e0-9811-c0f525cc08ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-83591" :question/problem "In what direction does the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{tan}⁡y+2{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ decrease most rapidly at the point $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4})?$" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $f(x,y)$ decreases most rapidly in the direction opposite to that of its gradient.\n\nSo, we compute $-∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-∇f(x,y) & =-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{tan}⁡y+2{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\text{ }i-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{tan}⁡y+2{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡y+4x-\\frac{1}{x})i-x{sec}^{2}⁡y\\text{ }j \\\\ -∇f(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)+4\\cdot 1-\\frac{1}{1})i-1\\cdot {sec}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =-4\\,i-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function decreases most rapidly in the direction of $-4\\,i-2\\,j.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bdec8d3-0363-5eab-8216-e13c1bc6dfc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32 y^{3} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 4 \\arctan{\\left(x \\right)} - \\frac{2 y}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563913} {:answer/id #uuid "3fde6af7-e556-5f3d-be08-5a96003cbd72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 y^{4} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{4 y}{x^{2} + 1} - \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563920} {:answer/id #uuid "7b18f342-7832-5070-80b5-ac6287b1e6ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 y^{4} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{4}{x^{2} + 1} + \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563932} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d2d702-1a45-5763-80bf-ddbc0c8e01fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 y^{4} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{4 y}{x^{2} + 1} + \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563943} {:answer/id #uuid "fb8bd3bb-d891-5b48-b7c5-d72caa5b2b4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 y^{4} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{4 y}{x^{2} + 1} + \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0d2d702-1a45-5763-80bf-ddbc0c8e01fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 y^{4} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{4 y}{x^{2} + 1} + \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563943} :answer-field/id #uuid "76582032-af87-5d6f-82c4-522f1be624eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "358908ba-e0d7-5631-bfea-bfcff1b40f32" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=8 y^{4} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}+4 y \\arctan{\\left(x \\right)}- \\frac{y^{2}}{x^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The notation ${f}_{x}$ denotes the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x.$\n\nWe differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8 y^{4} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}+4 y \\arctan{\\left(x \\right)}- \\frac{y^{2}}{x^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8 y^{4} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4 y \\arctan{\\left(x \\right)})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{y^{2}}{x^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =8 y^{4}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})+4 y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\arctan{\\left(x \\right)})-y^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{1}{x^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =8 y^{4}\\cdot \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}+4 y\\cdot \\frac{1}{x^{2} + 1}-y^{2}\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{2}{x^{3}}\\right) \\\\  & =8 y^{4} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{4 y}{x^{2} + 1} + \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]
